# Cloud Build: Test-in-Image Architecture

RULE: Quality gates run INSIDE the built Docker image. Never git-clone source or run tests outside the image in Cloud Build.
WHY: Tests the exact artifact that gets deployed. Prod parity, no GitHub token required, ~2-3 min faster.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md

Architecture:
  1. Pull unified-trading-library:latest base image (requires auth)
  2. Build service image (includes source + tests + dev deps via uv pip install .[dev])
  3. Run quality-gates.sh --no-fix --quick INSIDE the image
  4. Push image ONLY if tests pass

Library publishing pattern (idempotent):
  - Stores version→commit mapping in GCS before upload
  - Same commit → skip (idempotent rebuild)
  - Different commit → FAIL (require version bump in pyproject.toml)

NEVER:
  git clone inside Cloud Build steps
  Run pytest outside the Docker image
  Push image before tests pass
  Skip version validation for library publishing
